From ee99226def12e0214e3001d399827989f26834a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zortos293 <65777760+zortos293@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:41:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] input: build SDL3 with libusb on Windows for Switch 2
 controllers

Ports Eglantine PR #573 (cakezara): on MSVC the bundled SDL3 package has no
libusb, so SDL's Switch 2 driver is compiled out. Build SDL 3.4.20 from source
against the libusb external instead, with the two Switch 2 sensor fixes from
SDL release-3.4.x (b0bb2d01f, 5576a4ee3). Name the pad "Nintendo Switch 2 Pro
Controller", keep the GameCube adapter away from SDL's libusb path on Windows,
and add a udev rule for USB access on Linux.

Co-authored-by: capy-ai[bot] <230910855+capy-ai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
